  "variation": {
    "seeded": true,
    "notes": "Jet ripple, droplet paths, puddle shape and mist vary per cast. The 180 ms travel, the impact time and the fountain height stay fixed so the hit always lands at the same moment."
  },
  "director_notes": "Directed from a game-capture reference whose jet was a flat, blown-out white bar and whose splash read yellow-green over grass. Fixes: (1) the jet is mid-blue with only a thin white thread, so it reads as water on any background; (2) a 320 ms gather and a 180 ms visible travel replace the reference's instant on/off, so the hit has a cause; (3) the splash is a fountain that keeps spraying for the whole contact and falls back with gravity, plus mist, ripples and a puddle, so water has weight and leaves a mark. The reference's camera cuts are not copied: this is one continuous shot. Decals: a wide dark wet patch, a brighter puddle that spreads out (grow_ms) and splash droplets around it, all alpha-blended. The puddle and wet patch outlive the spell."
}
